    "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
    "senderName": "NWS San Diego CA",
    "headline": "Coastal Flood Warning issued October 27 at 12:53PM PDT until October 29 at 1:00PM PDT by NWS San Diego CA",
    "description": "* WHAT...Significant coastal flooding expected.\n\n* WHERE...San Diego County coastal areas and Orange County\nCoastal Areas.\n\n* WHEN...Until 1 PM PDT Thursday during high tides in the late\nmornings.\n\n* IMPACTS...Numerous roads may be closed. Low lying property\nincluding homes, businesses, and some critical infrastructure\nwill be inundated. Some shoreline erosion will occur in the\nlate mornings.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Coastal residents and managers of\ninfrastructure in the warned area should prepare for rising\nwater and take appropriate action to protect life and\nproperty. High tides each day will occur in the late morning.\nObserved high tides are 1.4 to 1.6 feet above astronomical\ntide predictions.",
    "instruction": "Take the necessary actions to protect flood-prone property. If\ntravel is required, do not drive around barricades or through\nwater of unknown depth.",
    "response": "Avoid",
    "note": null,
